From 9f73e4ed06fd2b203464c82c8eed4b84d37262e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(players): refresh local and inherited game modes

Bedrock can update the local actor before it appears in the player list.
Resolve that actor by its StartGame unique ID so Java receives the mode
event and can open the correct inventory.

Retain remote game types from spawn and player updates. A world-default
change must refresh inheriting Java profiles even outside render distance;
otherwise remote spectator visibility and interaction state remain stale.
Bind cached modes to both profile and actor identity, preserving list
refreshes and clearing removed or replaced actors.

Send only changed remote modes. Keep the existing local profile/event
updates and Java effective-mode fallback separate from native aim rules.
